{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"4043256d8ce6767d09a8896b7cfac7be1fd34f002eccdb48cb1186fec9ec38fa","digest":{"component_or_area":"grounding metric backend (Engine B)","key_entities":["src/rebar/grounding/engine_b_backends.py::_metric_invoke","src/rebar/grounding/engine_b_backends.py::_scc_files","rebar.builtin.smell.metric-oversize","scc --by-file","scc --format json","tests/unit/grounding/test_engine_b.py::test_metric_backend_requests_per_file_json_and_emits_only_over_cutoff"],"problem_keywords":["scc invocation","missing command flag","per-file JSON","metric backend","file matching"],"propositions":["The grounding metric backend invokes scc without the --by-file flag, causing scc to return language summaries with empty Files arrays instead of per-file entries.","The _scc_files parser depends on Files array entries and therefore yields no results, preventing the LOC threshold loop from executing and emitting any metric matches.","A present scc binary with files exceeding the 800-LOC threshold produces zero matches when invoked without --by-file, violating the documented detector contract.","Adding --by-file to the _metric_invoke scc command restores per-file JSON parsing and enables threshold-based file matching without changing Code field behavior or fail-open semantics."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787308334705271001,"uuid":"b3c12b26-2cab-48d0-8d3e-e10d384d6785"}